error: `Directory.openRoot` holds the thread until it is done, and an async function does not hold its thread
  `Directory.openRoot` waits for the disk
  the tasks of async functions share a few threads: one that holds its thread keeps the others from running
  --> error_open_root_in_async.sg:3:30
 3 |     var root = try Directory.openRoot(".")
   |                              ^^^^^^^^
  hint: `await Directory.openRootAsync(".")` does the same work without holding the thread
